From f25b8655845ca510e4c592a9599ea47106aae59a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:02:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] One basis per dashboard refresh (otel-chdb D30)

Every statement of a page load or dashboard refresh carries the page's
basis group (X-Otel-Basis-Group, derived from the page load and the
searched time range); the otel-chdb adapter pins one basis per group, so
the panels read the same rows while data keeps arriving and only a refresh
moves them. The API proxy forwards only well-formed basis headers. Each
result records the basis it was computed at, and the banner says whether
the page reads at one basis, several, or up to now.
